\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {9}{\ignorespaces V-Web (left; full-sample canonical run, shown as reference) vs Tempel+2014 FoF (right; $96{,}753$-spiral overlap) cross-validation: per-class CW fraction with $95\%$ Jeffreys binomial credible intervals, shared y-axis [0.43, 0.53]. Dashed reference is parity $f_{\rm  CW}\!=\!0.5$; dotted-red reference is the Paper~IV global $\bar  f_{\rm  CW}\!=\!0.4974$ classifier-monopole offset. The quantitative concordance statistic is computed like-for-like on the common overlap sample (\S  \ref {sec:tempel}): Tempel filament\_like $f_{\rm  CW}\!=\!0.4980$ ($n\!=\!12{,}360$) vs V-Web filament-on-overlap $f_{\rm  CW}\!=\!0.5009$ ($n\!=\!16{,}701$), a $0.29$\,pp (${\sim }0.5\sigma $) difference, statistically indistinguishable (supporting, not load-bearing; the primary cross-classifier validation is the on-DESI DESIVAST re-projection in \S  \ref {sec:desivast_primary}). Lower-$n$ classes scatter by counting statistics and classifier-definition mismatch (V-Web $\lambda _{\rm  th}\!=\!0$ vs Tempel discrete richness thresholds) but do not contradict the environmental-independence headline.}}{25}{figure.9}\protected@file@percent }
\newlabel{fig:tempel_overlay}{{9}{25}{V-Web (left; full-sample canonical run, shown as reference) vs Tempel+2014 FoF (right; $96{,}753$-spiral overlap) cross-validation: per-class CW fraction with $95\%$ Jeffreys binomial credible intervals, shared y-axis [0.43, 0.53]. Dashed reference is parity $f_{\rm CW}\!=\!0.5$; dotted-red reference is the Paper~IV global $\bar f_{\rm CW}\!=\!0.4974$ classifier-monopole offset. The quantitative concordance statistic is computed like-for-like on the common overlap sample (\S \ref {sec:tempel}): Tempel filament\_like $f_{\rm CW}\!=\!0.4980$ ($n\!=\!12{,}360$) vs V-Web filament-on-overlap $f_{\rm CW}\!=\!0.5009$ ($n\!=\!16{,}701$), a $0.29$\,pp (${\sim }0.5\sigma $) difference, statistically indistinguishable (supporting, not load-bearing; the primary cross-classifier validation is the on-DESI DESIVAST re-projection in \S \ref {sec:desivast_primary}). Lower-$n$ classes scatter by counting statistics and classifier-definition mismatch (V-Web $\lambda _{\rm th}\!=\!0$ vs Tempel discrete richness thresholds) but do not contradict the environmental-independence headline}{figure.9}{}}
